(a) whether Government is aware that tribal and women litigants often face denial of legal representation when their case is against the family members of an advocate registered in the same Bar Association, resulting in refusal by local advocates to accept the brief;
(b) whether such situations amount to denial of access to justice despite the availability of legal aid provisions;
(c) whether there exists any mechanism under the Legal Services Authorities framework to provide independent legal aid counsel from outside the concerned district or State; and
(d) the steps taken/proposed to ensure impartial legal representation to vulnerable litigants in such circumstances?

(a) the total number of enterprises registered under the Udyam Registration Portal in the State of Sikkim during the last three years, year-wise;
(b) the total number of projects assisted under the Prime Minister’s Employment Generation Programme (PMEGP) in Sikkim during the last three years along with estimated employment generated;
(c) the total number of loan guarantees approved under the Credit Guarantee Fund Trust for Micro and Small Enterprises (CGTMSE) in Sikkim during the last three years, year-wise; and
(d) steps taken by Government to improve MSME penetration and entrepreneurship development in hilly and border States like Sikkim?

(a) whether Government has taken any specific step or initiatives for the promotion, preservation and propagation of the Sanskrit language in the State of Sikkim;
(b) if so, the details thereof including financial assistance provided during the last three years and the current year;
(c) whether any Sanskrit schools, colleges, research centres or teacher training programmes are being supported by the Central Government in Sikkim; and
(d) the future roadmap or proposals, if any, to further strengthen Sanskrit education and awareness in the State, particularly among youth and educational institutions?

(a) whether the Agricultural and Processed Food Products Export Development Authority (APEDA) suspended Sikkim State Organic Certification Agency (SSOCA) for a period of one year starting from October 2024;
(b) if so, the reasons for such suspension;
(c) whether the said suspension/ban has been lifted as on date; and
(d) if not, the present status of the suspension and the steps taken or proposed to be taken by Government to restore organic certification activities in Sikkim?

(a) the current status of implementation of North Eastern Region Agri-Commodity e-Connect (NERACE) app, including the number of farmers, traders and agri-commodities onboarded since its launch in July 2024;
(b) the volume and value of agri-produce transactions facilitated through the platform and its impact on farmers’ income in Sikkim;
(c) the extent to which multilingual support and helpline services are being utilised by farmers across Sikkim; and
(d) the steps taken or proposed to expand the app’s outreach, integrate logistics and export linkages and strengthen digital market access for farmers in Sikkim?

(a) whether any Community Radio initiatives from the State of Sikkim have applied for or availed benefits under these schemes in the last five years;
(b) if so, the details thereof, including the number of applications received, sanctioned, and pending from Sikkim;
(c) whether Government proposes to expand or facilitate the setting up of additional Community Radio Stations in small and hilly States like Sikkim; and
(d) if so, the details of steps being taken or proposed to improve outreach, capacity building, and technical support for Community Radio in the State?

(a) whether Government has conducted any recent review regarding the resumption, expansion or strengthening of border trade through Nathula and if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether the Ministry has taken up, with the concerned authorities of neighbouring countries, the issues raised by the State Government of Sikkim relating to tourism, trade, border incidents or local livelihood concerns arising out of relations with China, Bhutan and Nepal; and
(c) the details of support being extended by the Ministry to ensure that Sikkim’s strategic, economic and development interests are safeguarded, in view of increasing geopolitical sensitivity in the region?

(a) whether the Ministry is considering support, financial assistance, priority treatment schemes for patients from Sikkim in tertiary-level care outside their State;
(b) the details of medical treatment facilities provided to the people of the State in AIIMS, other Central Government hospitals, any reserved quotas, special provisions or referral mechanisms;
(c) whether Government proposes to establish a dedicated helpdesk, facilitation centre or nodal officer in AIIMS and other major Central hospitals to support patients arriving from the State; and
(d) the steps taken by Government to enhance medical infrastructure in the State, so that patients are not compelled to travel long distances for advanced medical treatment?

(a) whether Government has any Centrally Sponsored Scheme (CSS) or specific programme for the construction, upgradation or renovation of District Guest Houses, Circuit Houses or Zilla Atithi Griha in the States, including small States like the State of Sikkim;
(b) if so, the details of such schemes, including eligibility criteria, funding pattern and the number of projects sanctioned during the last five years, State-wise;
(c) whether any proposal has been received from Government of the State of Sikkim for construction of a District Guest House or Zilla Atithi Griha under any Centrally Sponsored Scheme; and
(d) if so, the present status of proposals?

(a) whether the Ministry has received Annual Action Plans (AAPs) from Government of Sikkim during the last three years seeking assistance under the Mission for Integrated Development of Horticulture (MIDH) for establishment of cold storage facilities up to 5,000 MT capacity;
(b) if so, the year-wise details of the proposals submitted by Sikkim and the status of their approval;
(c) the total financial assistance sought by Sikkim under MIDH for cold storage infrastructure during the said period; and
(d) whether any proposals from Sikkim were pending, rejected, or returned for revision during the last three years?

(a) whether the Employment Exchange system, mandated under the Employment Exchanges (Compulsory Notification of Vacancies) Act, 1959, is not being effectively implemented in Sikkim;
(b) whether Government has received any report or representation regarding non-functioning or inadequate functioning of the Exchanges therein;
(c) the steps taken by the Ministry to ensure that all the States, including Sikkim, comply with the compulsory notification of vacancies by employers in both public and private sectors; and
(d) whether the Ministry proposes any special monitoring mechanism to operationalise and modernise the Exchanges, including digital platforms like National Career Service (NCS)?

(a) whether Government proposes to provide any special financial or technical assistance to small States like the State of Sikkim under centrally sponsored schemes such as Jal Jeevan Mission, Namami Gange Programme (for relevant tributaries), flood management and river rejuvenation projects;
(b) if so, the details thereof and the quantum of assistance extended to the State of Sikkim during the last five years; and
(c) whether Government will consider creating a separate policy or special category support for small and disaster-prone Himalayan States to ensure timely completion and sustainability of water-related infrastructure projects and if so, the timeframe for the same?

(a) whether the University Grants Commission has conducted any inquiry or regulatory action regarding the recognition, quality standards and functioning of large number of Universities registered in Sikkim;
(b) whether Government proposes to take steps to protect the rights of students enrolled in these institutions, including verification and public disclosure of the status of recognition of university, action against institutions violating UGC norms, establishment of grievance-redressal mechanisms for affected students to ensure that degrees issued by compliant institutions are fully valid nationwide; and 
(c) the corrective measures intended to prevent misuse of the higher-education registration process in small States like Sikkim?

(a) whether Government has taken note of the difficulties being reported in the registration of companies, filing of statutory returns and compliance procedures under MCA21 portal arising from connectivity issues and lack of facilitation centres in Sikkim;
(b) whether the Ministry proposes to establish a dedicated MCA facilitation in Sikkim to assist stakeholders, especially start-ups, MSMEs and cooperative entities;
(c) whether Government plans to provide any special exemptions, relaxations or hand-holding support for entities in Sikkim; and
(d) the details of steps taken or proposed to strengthen corporate governance, ease of doing business and digital filing efficiency in Sikkim?

(a) whether the works are being carried out under the Non-Lapsable Central Pool of Resources (NLCPR), North East Special Infrastructure Development Schemes (NESIDS) and Hill Area Development Programme (HADP) in the North Eastern States, particularly in Sikkim;
(b) if so, the details and current status, scheme-wise thereof; and
(c) the details of the central funds allocated and utilized during the last five years including current year, State-wise?

(a) whether all the States are members of National Foundation for Teachers' Welfare (NFTW);
(b) whether NFTW have received any application for registration from Education Department, Government of Sikkim for the teachers of Sikkim to National Foundation for Teachers' Welfare; 
(c) if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor; and 
(d) what are the various benefits under this scheme that a registered State can avail?

(a) whether the Companies Act, 2013 is applicable in the State of Sikkim, if so, the details thereof and the number of companies registered after the implementation of Companies Act, 2013, whether there is not a single company registered in the State, the details thereof;
(b) whether the registration of company in Sikkim is required to be done under the existing Sikkim Registration of Companies Act, 1961 or whether it is compulsory to be registered as per Companies Act, 2013; and
(c) the details thereof and the reasons for diluting the Sikkim Registration of Companies Act, 1961 protected by Article 371(F) of our Constitution?

(a) the current status of the scheme for supplying gas to the households through pipeline by Government in the State of Sikkim; 
(b) whether the issues being faced in laying of gas pipeline in the Himalayan areas of the State of Sikkim parliamentary constituency are in the cognizance of Government; 
(c) if so, the steps being taken by Government to resolve such issues; and 
(d) the time by when the work of gas pipeline is likely to be completed in the State of Sikkim?

(a) whether Government has provided any financial support to establish solar and wind energy plants in the country;
(b) if so, the details of operational solar and wind energy plants in the State of Sikkim; 
(c) the loans and subsidy extended through Government and Power Finance Companies like REC Ltd., PFC Ltd., etc., to establish renewable energy plants and the current status of these plants in the State of Sikkim; and 
(d) the steps taken by Government to harness renewable energy from various unconventional energy sources in Sikkim along with the target fixed for 2030?

(a) the total length of roads constructed under the Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY) in the last five years in Sikkim, year-wise;
(b) the budget allocated and spent on PMGSY in the current financial year;
(c) the impact of PMGSY on rural connectivity and economic development, particularly in Sikkim; and
(d) the measures taken to ensure the quality and durability of roads constructed under PMGSY?

(a) whether Government has taken any measures for resumption of the Nathu La border trade; 
(b) whether Government intends to introduce new protocols and emergency response systems to further bolster security in this region;
(c) the steps taken by Government towards resumption of the Nathu La border trade; and
(d) whether Government is formulating any policy for better management of trade, and effective support for economically weaker class of traders resided in remote border village of Indo- China Border ?

(a) whether the revised Livestock Health and Disease Control Programme (LHDCP) has effectively reduced the spread of major livestock diseases like Lumpy Skin disease (LSD), if so, the details thereof; 
(b) the details of disease outbreaks reported during last three years in Sikkim despite implementation of the programme;
(c) the steps taken to ensure quality and availability of veterinary vaccines under this programme; 
(d) whether there is a shortage of veterinary officers, veterinary hospitals, dispensaries and mobile veterinary units in State of Sikkim especially in rural areas; and
(e) the current veterinarian-to-livestock ratio in the country and whether it meets the recommended standards?

(a) the details of allocation of wheat, rice, edible oil, kerosene etc. made to the States of the North Eastern Region (NER) during the last three years till-date, State-wise particularly in Sikkim;
(b) whether it is a fact that the quota of above item released to NER are inadequate;
(c) if so, the reasons therefor; and
(d) the steps taken by Government in this regard?

(a) the details of the funds allocated and released for various educational schemes rolled out for minorities in the country during each of the last three years, State/UT-wise especially in Sikkim;
(b) the details of the funds allocated and released to all six districts of Sikkim for implementation of such schemes during the last three years; and
(c) the number of who applied and benefitted under such education schemes in Sikkim during the the last three years, scheme-wise?

(a) the total funds allocated and released for rural infrastructure projects under the Shyama Prasad Mukherji Rurban Mission (SPMRM) in Sikkim over the last three years; 
(b) the number of rural clusters developed under SPMRM in the State of Sikkim, district-wise;
(c) whether Government has identified any challenges in the implementation of this scheme, particularly in land slide-affected districts; and 
(d) the steps being taken to expedite rural infrastructure development in disaster-prone areas?

(a) the details of the activities carried out for the development of cultural sites in the State of Sikkim since 2020, year-wise;
(b) the details of the total amount allocated, spent and progress made with reference to above, year-wise and cultural site-wise for Sikkim from 2020 till date; and 
(c) whether Government has implemented any digital or technological initiatives, such as virtual tours or augmented reality experiences, to enhance the accessibility and awareness of cultural sites in Sikkim, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether it is a fact that Government has decided to construct 10,000 Anganwadi buildings every year in the country i.e. 50,000 in the coming five years under Mission Poshan 2.0;
(b) the Anganwadi Centres identified which does not have their own buildings in Sikkim, the details thereof, district-wise;
(c) the number of selected Anganwadis from Sikkim and by when the identified Anganwadis are going to be completed; and
(d) the details of funds released in 2023-2024 and 2024-2025 and utilization of funds and status of construction of Anganwadi buildings in Sikkim?

(a) whether Government has taken any step towards genetic improvement and preservation of Yak in the State of Sikkim; 
(b) whether Government provides any financial assistance to yak-herding communities; 
(c) if so, the details thereof including the criteria fixed for availing financial assistance; and 
(d) the details of steps taken by Government policy to overcome impacts of climate change and other socio-economic drivers and whether there has been a waning interest in yak farming?

(a) the details of schemes/projects initiated for the development of the handloom and handicraft sectors in rural areas over the last five years, particularly in Sikkim; 
(b) the funds allocated and utilized under these schemes, State-wise, with a focus on Sikkim; 
(c) the number of beneficiaries, especially woman, under these schemes, State-wise, particularly in Sikkim; and
 (d) whether Government plans to implement specific schemes for the development of handloom and handicraft sectors targeted towards ST communities?

(a) whether Pakyong airport since its commissioning in 2018, is rendered totally non operational since May 2024 due to technical reasons;
(b) if so, the efforts made by Government to improve potential operations of the Pakyong Airport;
(c) whether Government will have any specific plan to resume flying operations in Pakyong Airport ;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) if not, the reasons therefor?
bs

(a) whether it is a fact that Sikkim's Organic Certification Body suspension over controversial White Rice exports is a major blow to Sikkim's organic agriculture sector;
(b) whether the Agriculture and Processed Food Products Export Development Authority (APEDA) has suspended Sikkim's organic certification body over a scandal;
(c) if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor; and
(d) the action taken by Government in this regard?

(a) the aims and objectives of Bharat Dal Utpadan Swavalamban Abhiyan in the country;
(b) to what extent this helps push pulse production, meet buffer norms and make our country self-sufficient in pulse production, State/UT-wise including Sikkim;
(c) whether it is a fact that Sikkim has not been included in the Bharat Dal Scheme; and 
(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the aims and objectives of Bharat Dal Utpadan Swavalamban Abhiyan in the country;
(b) to what extent this helps to push pulse production, meet buffer norms and make our country self-sufficient in pulse production, State/UT-wise including Sikkim;
(c) whether it is a fact that the State of Sikkim has not been included in the Bharat Dal Schemes; and
(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the details of the present requirement and supply of drinking water, per capita, per day, in each State of the North East, especially in the State of Sikkim;
(b) whether all the habitations in the country are getting drinking water as per their requirement including the State;
(c) if so, the details thereof, if not, the reasons therefor; and
(d) the steps taken/proposed to be taken by Government to ensure availability of requisite quantity of drinking water in the country?

(a) the details of the works done for conservation and enhancement of indigenous breeds of cows in the country under the Rashtriya Gokul Mission (RGM) during each of the last three years, State-wise/UT-wise; 
(b) the number of Gokul Grams sanctioned in North Eastern States particularly in Sikkim; 
(c) whether Government has included the Yak on this Rashtriya Kamdhenu Aayog (RKA) in the country; 
(d) if not, the reasons therefor; and 
(e) the steps taken/proposed to be taken by Government for the protection and development of the livestock population as well as for the conservation of indigenous breeds in the country?

(a) the storage capacity of Food Corporation of India (FCI) at present, State-wise especially in the State of Sikkim;
(b) whether Government has increased the storage capacity of FCI in Sikkim during the last three years and the current year and if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether FCI hires warehouses from different Central and State agencies based on the storage gap assessment and if so, the details of such agencies in Sikkim;
(d) the amount spent on these agencies annually; and
(e) the total quantity of foodgrains wasted in FCI’s own and rented warehouses during the last three years, State/warehouse-wise?

(a) whether several societies in North-Eastern States including Sikkim to which land has been allocatted at concessional rates have failed to construct buildings for schools;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether any time limit has been given to them to construct the school buildings in Sikkim;
(d) if so, the details thereof;
(e) whether Government has taken any steps against the errant societies; and
(f) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether a proposal to provide a revised rescue package for Air India is under consideration;
(b) if so, the details thereof; and
(c) the circumstances which have necessitated such a proposal?

(a) the details of Ayush treatment facilities available in rural and tribal areas of the country particularly in the State of Sikkim, State/UT-wise;
(b) the funds allocated during the last three years and current year; and
(c) the efforts being made by Government to increase these facilities and facilitate its expansion in the country, specially in the State of Sikkim?

(a) the details of salient features of AYUSH health centres in North Eastern (NE) States particularly in Sikkim;
(b) the details of set up/proposed and running AYUSH health centres in NE region, particularly in Sikkim, State/UT-wise; and
(c) the details of steps taken for the development of AYUSH centers at district level in the State of Sikkim, district wise?

(a) whether Government propose to implement Centrally Sponsored Scheme (CSS) for de-addiction centres at village Panchayat level in the country, including North-eastern States, particularly in the State of Sikkim;
(b) if so, the details thereof along with the said centres proposed to be opened during the last three years and current year, State-wise/UT-wise, particularly in Sikkim, location-wise;
(c) whether any fund has been allocated in this regard during the last three years including current year; and
(d) if so, the details thereof State-wise, including Sikkim?

(a) whether Government has not been able to develop rural tourism in North-Eastern Region including Sikkim to the desired extent though country has a huge potential, if so, details thereof and the reasons therefor;
(b) objectives and the success achieved since the inception of rural tourism schemes in Sikkim;
(c) criteria adopted for providing central financial assistance for development of rural sites; and
(d) details of funds sanctioned/released/utilized for rural tourism projects out of the proposals received during each of the last three years and the current year, indicating the status of completed projects, State /UT-wise?

(a) the major steps taken by Government to institutionalize market links to provide maximum benefits to the beneficiaries under North Eastern rural livelihood projects;
(b) whether North East livelihood project has had a great impact on employment of rural population of North-Eastern Region, particularly in Sikkim;
(c) if so, the details thereof along with the number of various other schemes being implemented by Government to make this project more effective; and
(d) whether Government is working on any other new schemes for the development of North-Eastern States and Sikkim and if so, the details thereof?
J

(a) whether Government has received any proposal from the State Government of Sikkim, pertaining to the inclusion of Lepcha, Bhutia and Limbu languages in the list of Eight Schedule of the Constitution of India;
(b) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor ; and
(c) the details of action taken by Government on the proposal of the State Government and the present status of the proposal thereof?

(a) number and percentage of students who availed education loans from Bhartiya Mahila Bank (BMB), total loan amount sanctioned and disbursed during the last three years including current year and their utilization, in Sikkim;
(b) the present rate of interest being charged by BMB on education loan in the country;
(c) whether BMB charges lower interest rate from girl students in comparison to male students, if so, the reasons therefor along with steps taken by Government to remove this disparity; and
(d) whether BMB has any proposal to grant loans to woman Self Help Groups in Sikkim?
KG

(a) whether Government has taken any measures for infrastructure development to ensure the security of pilgrims in Kailash Mansarovar;
(b) whether Government intends to introduce new protocols and emergency response systems to further bolster security in this region;
(c) the steps taken by Government towards protection of environment, better health and medical facilities and preservation of culture in this pilgrimage destination;
(d) whether Government is formulating any policy for better management of pilgrim, quotas and effective support for economically weaker pilgrims; and
(e) the steps taken by Government to raise awareness among potential pilgrims, specially in Sikkim and North-Eastern States?

(a) whether there has been a rise in incidents of delayed flights of almost all major airlines in the country during the last one year till date;
(b) the efforts being made by Government to ensure the maintenance of time schedule of flights;
(c) whether any new mechanism has been developed to avoid delay of flights, especially during winter seasons;
(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; and
(e) the corrective majors undertaken by Government during the last three years to improve passenger amenities at airports across country, particularly in North Eastern Region including Pakyong Airport (Sikkim) and Bagdogra Airport (West Bengal)?

(a) whether Government will include the 12 left-out communities in Sikkim in the Scheduled Tribes (ST) list;
(b) the steps taken to expedite their inclusion;
(c) the expected timeline for the inclusion of these communities;
(d) the manner in which Government will address the socio-economic challenges faced by these communities in the interim; and
(e) the manner in which Government will ensure that the benefits of inclusion reach all members of these communities?

(a) whether there is a consistent demand from Government of Sikkim to transfer the stretch between Sevoke and Rangpo (National Highway No. 10) from Public Works Department (PWD), West Bengal, to National Highways and Infrastructure Development Corporation Ltd. (NHIDCL), which is currently maintaining the Rangpo to Gangtok (40 km) stretch for efficient management of the Highway;
(b) if so, whether Government will transfer the stretch between Sevoke and Rangpo to NHIDCL for better maintenance and management;
(c) if so, by when, this transfer will be executed; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government intends to provide assistance and incentives to tea growers in Sikkim, given that Sikkim is encouraging tea plantation in all six districts;
(b) if so, the types of support and financial assistance that will be provided; and
(c) whether there are any specific programs or initiatives planned to promote Sikkim's tea industry on a national and international scale?

(a) whether it is a fact that there is frequent cancellation of flights to and fro Pakyong Airport of Sikkim particularly during monsoon season;
(b) whether instead of cancelling the flights to and fro Pakyong Airport altogether from stations of departure during the raining season, flights can be rerouted to Bagdogra Airport to provide opportunity to the tourists and local people to avail air services without significant loss of time and money;
(c) if so, the response of Government thereto; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government plans to project Sikkim as a model State in the country in organic farming;
(b) whether any assistance is provided to Sikkim in sustaining the status of fully organic farming State, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) if not, whether Government will assist Sikkim in adopting new innovative techniques for organic farming and reducing the cost of production to encourage organic farming in the country?

(a) whether Pakyong Airport since its commissioning in 2018 is marred by flight cancellations due to poor visibility particularly during Monsoon season;
(b) if so, the efforts made by Government to improve potential operations of the Pakyong Airport in low visibility;
(c) whether Government will conduct a feasibility study for installation of GAGAN based navigation system and/or Instrument Landing System (ILS) at Pakyong airport to enhance the flying operations during low visibility conditions;
(d) if so, details thereof; and
(e) if not, the reasons therefor?
